WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:58.800 --> 00:01:04.640
Let's start with the big picture. Ethiopia is&nbsp;
about the size of France and Spain combined.

00:01:04.640 --> 00:01:10.080
It has the second biggest population in Africa,&nbsp;
with lots of different ethnic groups. There's

00:01:10.080 --> 00:01:16.080
a federal government based in Addis Ababa, led&nbsp;
by prime minister Abiy Ahmed. And there are 11

00:01:16.080 --> 00:01:19.920
regions. They're mostly divided&nbsp;
according to different ethnic groups,

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:25.440
and each region has its own government. Tigray&nbsp;
way up north is where most of the fighting has

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:31.760
been happening over the past year. It's led by&nbsp;
the Tigray People's Liberation Front - the TPLF.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:37.360
Now all this started because of a power&nbsp;
struggle between the TPLF and the Federal

00:01:37.360 --> 00:01:43.600
government. But it's gone way beyond that&nbsp;
now. 

00:02:06.560 --> 00:02:11.760
What you have&nbsp;
to understand is the TPLF used to run things.

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:17.920
They dominated Ethiopia's national politics&nbsp;
for nearly 30 years as the main party in

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:23.040
a coalition government, although Tigrayans&nbsp;
only make up six percent of the population.

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:31.040
It was a time of huge economic growth, but the TPLF&nbsp;
were also accused of being autocratic and corrupt.

00:02:34.240 --> 00:02:40.640
In 2018, huge protests brought them down and&nbsp;
swept Abiy Ahmed into power. And right after

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:46.720
he was elected, he made some big changes. He&nbsp;
freed thousands of political prisoners who'd

00:02:46.720 --> 00:02:52.720
been thrown in jail by the previous government, and&nbsp;
surprised everyone with a peace deal with Eritrea.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:58.240
That's what he got his Nobel Peace Prize for.&nbsp;
He also tried to centralize the government more.

00:02:58.240 --> 00:03:03.840
He created a new national party that brought&nbsp;
together the main ethnic political groups,

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:11.840
but the TPLF refused to take part. And they were&nbsp;
suspicious of Abiy's big plans to open up politics

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:17.600
and the economy. There was a sense he was trying to&nbsp;
boost the power of the government in Addis Ababa

00:03:17.600 --> 00:03:24.560
at the expense of the regions. 

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:33.600
So you had&nbsp;all this political jocking. And then in 2020, there

00:03:33.600 --> 00:03:38.480
were supposed to be federal and regional elections.
But the government delayed them, saying it was

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:44.400
because of Covid. That didn't go down well with&nbsp;
the TPLF. 

00:03:55.840 --> 00:04:00.160
And that's when the fighting started.

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:08.640
Forces loyal to the TPLF attacked a government&nbsp;
military base in Tigray, then Abiy sent in troops.

00:04:09.280 --> 00:04:15.360
At first government forces had the upper hand. They&nbsp;
quickly took control of Tigray's capital Mekelle

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:22.240
and Abiy declared victory. But it wasn't over. The&nbsp;
TPLF forces kept fighting back, and you also had

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:26.800
Eritrean troops joining in. They came over the&nbsp;
border in the north to fight on the federal

00:04:26.800 --> 00:04:32.400
government's side. But by the end of June and&nbsp;
despite Eritrean involvement, there was a complete

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:39.280
reversal. The TPLF were back in control of Mekelle&nbsp;
and most of Tigray, and they didn't stop there. They

00:04:39.280 --> 00:04:45.040
pushed into the neighboring regions of Amhara&nbsp;
and Afar. Then there was another big development.

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:50.640
This time in the Oromia region, where there's&nbsp;
an armed group called the Oromo Liberation Army 

00:04:50.640 --> 00:04:57.040
- the OLA. They have their own issues with Abiy.&nbsp;
They decided to ally themselves with the TPLF,

00:04:57.040 --> 00:05:02.560
which means now you've got a kind of opposition&nbsp;
alliance that wants to defeat Abiy. Several groups

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:08.640
from other regions say they've joined too. The OLA&nbsp;
are fighting from the south, and the Tigrayans from

00:05:08.640 --> 00:05:14.880
the north. And they both say they're determined&nbsp;
to push towards the capital. Now when the TPLF

00:05:14.880 --> 00:05:20.960
forces took control of two strategic towns in&nbsp;
late October, that threat suddenly looked pretty

00:05:20.960 --> 00:05:26.320
serious. But by early December, the government&nbsp;
said its forces had recaptured those towns.

00:05:26.320 --> 00:05:30.640
So the military balance seems to be&nbsp;
shifting again. 

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:40.160
So that's how the&nbsp;
fighting has played out so far. But what about the

00:05:40.160 --> 00:05:48.000
civilians? Well it's been devastating and brutal.&nbsp;
All sides involved have been accused of atrocities.

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:08.880
More than two million people have been forced to&nbsp;
leave their homes to escape the fighting. There

00:06:08.880 --> 00:06:14.880
are estimates that hundreds are dying every day in&nbsp;
Tigray because there isn't enough food. And the UN

00:06:14.880 --> 00:06:21.360
says millions are at risk of starvation. 

00:06:21.360 --> 00:06:27.680
Only a trickle of food has&nbsp;
been getting through - nowhere near what's needed.

00:06:28.400 --> 00:06:34.400
Both the government and TPLF forces are accused of&nbsp;
restricting aid deliveries into areas they control.

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:41.440
There have also been reports of horrific&nbsp;
massacres. Like in Axum, a town in Tigray

00:06:41.440 --> 00:06:46.240
where Eritrean forces killed hundreds of&nbsp;
people according to Amnesty International.

00:06:46.240 --> 00:06:52.720
And in Mai Kadra another town in Tigray where&nbsp;
up to 600 civilians were reportedly killed.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:08.720
Witnesses later said that forces linked&nbsp;
to the TPLF were responsible. 

00:07:14.880 --> 00:07:20.880
To end the fighting, what Ethiopia

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:26.720
really needs is some kind of negotiated settlement.
But right now, there's no sign that anyone is

00:07:26.720 --> 00:07:34.320
willing to come to the table. Let alone make any&nbsp;
concessions. If you found that useful, we have loads

00:07:34.320 --> 00:07:43.360
more explainers on the Start Here playlist&nbsp;
on Al Jazeera's youtube channel. Check it out.

